From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:27:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Parse ::-webkit-input-placeholder as ::placeholder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chromium still matches the WebKit spelling as an alias, and older
stylesheets (todomvc's among them) style placeholders with it and the
-moz- form only. Without the alias those rules were dropped, which
only went unnoticed while paint forced every placeholder italic and
dim on its own.

beep-boop-🤖
---
 servo/selector_parser.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/servo/selector_parser.rs b/servo/selector_parser.rs
index f08a8c2..d9e43a7 100644
--- a/servo/selector_parser.rs
+++ b/servo/selector_parser.rs
@@ -715,6 +715,9 @@ impl<'a, 'i> ::selectors::Parser<'i> for SelectorParser<'a> {
             "details-content" => DetailsContent,
             "color-swatch" => ColorSwatch,
             "placeholder" => Placeholder,
+            // The WebKit spelling that Chromium still accepts as
+            // an alias, and that todomvc-era stylesheets use on their own.
+            "-webkit-input-placeholder" => Placeholder,
             "-servo-text-control-inner-container" => {
                 if !self.in_user_agent_stylesheet() {
                     return Err(ParseError::custom(SelectorParseErrorKind::UnexpectedIdent))
